      <Desc>Daily instruction consists of approximately 1.25 hours dedicated to mathematics in the morning followed by about 1.5 hours for English Language Arts. Additionally around 1.25 hours is allocated for each of the subjects of science and social studies history. This structured schedule is designed to ensure that students thoroughly understand the essential concepts and skills required to meet their grade-level standards. Students engage in both subject-specific and interdisciplinary assignments allowing them to reinforce their understanding and apply their knowledge in diverse contexts. The CLP program employs a curriculum that is aligned with grade-level expectations as well as Common Core and Next Generation Science Standards NGSS to help students achieve their academic goals. This approach prepares them for successful completion of each grade and adequately equips them for advancement to the next level.</Desc>
